      "problem": "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)={2}^{y-2x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that\n\n- $y-2x$ is defined for all $x$ and $y,$ and\n\n- ${2}^{g(x,y)}$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, ${2}^{y-2x}$ is defined for all values of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the domain of $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane.",
